 "_readme": "Respondent panel (protocol Section 6.2). Prices: US$ per 1M tokens, 8 Nov 2026 snapshot; re-check before runs. Routing is per developer: Anthropic and OpenAI models go direct with AC_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY / AC_OPENAI_API_KEY (no router moderation layer), and all other API models go through one OpenRouter project account (AC_OPENROUTER_API_KEY). Model 14 (Gemini 4 Argon) left the study by decision D17 (12 Nov 2026): its price rises above the cap of Section 3.2 on 1 Dec 2026. No model uses the Gemini API (decision D2 had moved model 14 there on 11 Nov 2026). Reasoning effort is pinned to each model's snapshot default (8 Nov 2026), except that a 'max' default is lowered to 'high' (GLM-5.3-Flash, Kimi K3.1 Pro) for cost and truncation; effort vocabularies differ by provider, so no common level exists. Output caps include reasoning tokens. prompt_subset selects the frozen subset (src/subsets.py); receives_harmful per PI decision of 8 Nov 2026. API models stay disabled until the pilot. Respondent seed 20261126 for every model (decision D18, 12 Nov 2026; the answers of 7-9 Nov used 20261107 and are not used): sent to OpenRouter models too (ignored where unsupported); provider_order is filled from the pilot's served_provider before the main run, with allow_fallbacks false, and the change is logged as a config change. Decision D16 (11 Nov 2026): every model reached through OpenRouter is pinned to one zero-retention endpoint ('provider_order', no fallback), chosen by the rule recorded in docs/PI_DECISIONS.md, and its prices are those of that endpoint in the snapshot of 11 Nov 2026 (data/selection/2026-11-11).",
